0..80 Comment "// A doubly recursive function of twelve levels answers true without allocating."
81..83 Comment "//"
84..164 Comment "// Boespflug, Dénès and Grégoire make 2^27 trivial calls, so the run measures"
165..239 Comment "// calls without garbage collection. Their native code gained most on that"
240..252 Comment "// workload."
253..255 Comment "//"
256..330 Comment "// Each level calls the level below twice and answers a constant. The path"
331..368 Comment "// reads the answer at twelve levels."
369..371 Comment "//"
372..450 Comment "// - see: Boespflug, Dénès and Grégoire, _Full Reduction at Full Throttle_,"
451..482 Comment "//   CPP 2011, § 4, RecNoAlloc"
483..520 Comment "// - see: #2282 — the benchmark set"
522..543 Comment "// The free naturals."
